<mujoco model="keyboard_aluminum_plate">
  <!--
    AME 547 - Keyboard Assembly Cell Simulation
    Component: Aluminum Switch Plate (75% Layout, 84-key)

    Reference: Keychron K2 V3
    Material: Aluminum (6061-T6)

    Dimensions:
      317mm × 107mm × 1.5mm
      Fits inside case interior (319mm × 109mm) with 1mm tolerance each side
      Tight fit for robot placement — easy insertion, no slop

    Coordinate convention: matches bottom_case.xml
      +X → keyboard length (left to right)
      +Y → keyboard width (front to back, rear = +Y)
      +Z → up

    Body origin: BOTTOM FACE of plate
      Stack position:
        Sound foam top z_world  = 0.01310m
        Plate bottom z_world    = 0.01310m
        Plate center z_world    = 0.01310 + 0.00075 = 0.01385m
        Plate top z_world       = 0.01310 + 0.00150 = 0.01460m
        Body pos z              = 0.01310m

    Geometry strategy: Option C (primitive solid box, no cutouts)
      - Plate collision geom: contype=0, conaffinity=0 (non-colliding)
      - Switch insertion driven by site coordinates only
      - Upgrade to Option A (tiled box with real gaps) post April 18
      - Upgrade to mesh visual post April 18

    Switch cutout sites:
      - 84 sites representing Cherry MX switch hole centers
      - Standard MX grid: 19.05mm per U
      - Grid centered on plate: left margin = 6.1mm each side
      - Site type: cylinder, radius=0.003m
      - Site Z = plate top face = +0.00150m (body local)
      - Named by key function

    Screw hole sites:
      - 4 corner holes matching case screw boss positions
      - 4 additional center holes
      - Site type: cylinder, radius=0.0015m (M3 screw)

    Material properties:
      rgba    : brushed aluminum silver
      density : 2700 kg/m³
      Mass    : 317×107×1.5mm × 2.7g/cm³ ≈ 138g

    Robot placement:
      Robot 1 (UR5e, Station 1)
      Vacuum gripper on top face, centered
      Lowered straight down into case interior
  -->

